WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:06.801
Rose had trouble sleeping that night. She was eager to learn more about the mystery of Oliver's family.

2
00:00:06.802 --> 00:00:12.705
But Nancy had come to her in confidence and trusted her with the information that Monks and Oliver were brothers.

3
00:00:12.706 --> 00:00:18.610
Nancy's manner had touched Rose's heart, and Rose hoped that somehow she could help the miserable young woman.

4
00:00:18.611 --> 00:00:22.856
But Rose also loved Oliver, and there wasn't much time to help him.

5
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:31.205
Mrs. Maylie, Oliver, and Rose were going to be in London for only two more days. Then they would be traveling to the coast for several weeks.

6
00:00:31.206 --> 00:00:43.681
"I have to make a plan that can be executed in 48 hours!" Rose told herself. She sat up in bed, wide awake. "Or perhaps I can postpone our journey without causing suspicion!"

7
00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:51.665
Dr. Losberne was also staying with them at the London hotel. But Rose was well acquainted with the excellent gentleman's impetuosity.

8
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:58.244
If he learned that Nancy was the one who had captured Oliver for Fagin, he'd scour the city until he found her.

9
00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:12.585
"Then who knows what rash act Dr. Losberne might commit," Rose murmured. "No, I can't tell him. I also can't confide in my aunt because the first thing she'll do is consult Dr. Losberne. Maybe I could write to Harry."

10
00:01:12.586 --> 00:01:17.641
But then she remembered the last time she'd seen Harry, when she'd refused his marriage proposal.

11
00:01:17.642 --> 00:01:24.903
Tears came to her eyes. Still uncertain what to do, Rose lay down and finally fell asleep.

12
00:01:24.904 --> 00:01:33.387
The next morning she reluctantly decided to consult Harry. She sat with pen and paper, trying to write, but she couldn't think of what to say.

13
00:01:33.388 --> 00:01:41.300
Just then Oliver burst into her room. He had been out walking with Mr. Giles, and his face was flushed.

14
00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:44.395
"What's wrong?" asked Rose in alarm.

15
00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:53.467
"I hardly know where to begin," Oliver said breathlessly. "I've seen him! At last you'll know that I was telling you the truth."

16
00:01:53.468 --> 00:01:56.546
"Who are you talking about?" asked Rose.

17
00:01:56.547 --> 00:02:00.014
"The gentleman who was so good to me. Mr. Brownlow."

18
00:02:00.015 --> 00:02:05.784
"Where did you see him?" Rose laid down her pen, all thoughts of her letter forgotten.

19
00:02:05.785 --> 00:02:16.752
"Getting out of a coach and going into a house. I was trembling so much that I couldn't speak to him. But Mr. Giles asked a servant whether Mr. Brownlow lives there and he does!"

20
00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:26.419
Oliver showed Rose a scrap of paper. "Here's his address. Oh, dear me! What shall I do when I see him?"

21
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:38.252
"Quick!" said Rose. "Find someone to fetch us a coach and be ready to go with me in a few minutes. I'll tell my aunt that we're going out, but I won't say anything more. Now hurry!"

22
00:02:38.253 --> 00:02:42.340
In just over five minutes, they were on their way to Mr. Brownlow's house.

23
00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:47.403
Rose left Oliver in the coach under the pretense of preparing Mr. Brownlow for his arrival.

24
00:02:47.404 --> 00:02:51.641
A servant led her upstairs to a room, where Mr. Brownlow was sitting.

25
00:02:51.642 --> 00:03:01.070
"I have some news that will no doubt surprise you," said Rose after Mr. Brownlow had invited her to sit. "You once took an interest in a young friend of mine."

26
00:03:01.071 --> 00:03:05.055
"Indeed, who is that?" Mr. Brownlow was intrigued.

27
00:03:05.056 --> 00:03:06.832
"Oliver Twist."

28
00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:12.801
Mr. Brownlow was astonished to hear that name again. "What has become of him?"

29
00:03:12.802 --> 00:03:21.983
Rose told Mr. Brownlow everything that had happened to Oliver since that fateful day when he left for the bookseller's. But she did not share what Nancy had told her.

30
00:03:21.984 --> 00:03:29.197
"I'm very happy to hear this news of Oliver. Very happy. But you haven't told me where he is now."

31
00:03:29.198 --> 00:03:31.864
"He's waiting in a coach at the door."

32
00:03:31.865 --> 00:03:34.864
"At my door?" cried the old gentleman.

33
00:03:34.865 --> 00:03:39.292
With that he hurried from the room, down the stairs, and into the coach.

34
00:03:39.293 --> 00:03:44.435
"Oliver!" exclaimed Mr. Brownlow. "I knew you'd come back!"

35
00:03:44.436 --> 00:03:50.943
Overcome by tears of happiness, Oliver could not speak, but he embraced Mr. Brownlow.

36
00:03:50.944 --> 00:03:54.602
Hand in hand, they returned to the room where Rose was waiting.

37
00:03:54.603 --> 00:04:01.760
"There's someone else whom we should not forget." Mr. Brownlow rang the bell, summoning his housekeeper.

38
00:04:01.761 --> 00:04:08.753
Mrs. Bedwin responded to the bell at once. Dropping a curtsy to Mr. Brownlow, she waited for his orders.

39
00:04:08.754 --> 00:04:15.165
"Can't you see why I've summoned you?" Mr. Brownlow said somewhat crossly. "Put on your glasses."

40
00:04:15.166 --> 00:04:24.324
The old lady rummaged in her pocket. But Oliver could not wait for her to find her glasses. He ran to her and sprang into her arms.

41
00:04:24.325 --> 00:04:28.498
"My innocent boy!" she exclaimed as she hugged him.

42
00:04:28.499 --> 00:04:31.744
"My dear nurse!" cried Oliver.

43
00:04:31.745 --> 00:04:45.157
"I knew you would come back. How well you look! The same sweet face, but not so pale. The same gentle eyes, but not so sad. Where have you been?"

44
00:04:45.158 --> 00:04:47.895
Oliver began to tell his story.

45
00:04:47.896 --> 00:04:51.784
"I must speak to you alone," Rose whispered to Mr. Brownlow.

46
00:04:51.785 --> 00:04:57.142
He led her into another room, where she revealed to him what Nancy had told her.

47
00:04:57.143 --> 00:05:01.641
Rose also explained why she could not tell her aunt or Dr. Losberne.

48
00:05:01.642 --> 00:05:11.371
"A wise decision," said Mr. Brownlow. "Leave Dr. Losberne to me. I will call at the hotel this evening at eight o'clock and explain everything to him."

49
00:05:11.372 --> 00:05:17.554
Rose and Oliver soon had to return to the hotel, with Oliver promising to visit Mrs. Bedwin again.

50
00:05:17.555 --> 00:05:26.363
That night Mr. Brownlow met with Dr. Losberne, Mrs. Maylie, and Rose. Oliver was left alone in the next room, so he wouldn't hear what was said.

51
00:05:26.364 --> 00:05:35.260
Dr. Losberne was every bit as angry as Rose had feared. As soon as he heard Nancy's story, he was halfway out the door, threatening to track her down.

52
00:05:35.261 --> 00:05:39.530
Somehow Mr. Brownlow managed to stop him from going to the police.

53
00:05:39.531 --> 00:05:44.443
"So what are we supposed to do now?" Dr. Losberne said impatiently.

54
00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:50.093
"We need to find out who Oliver's parents were and discover if Nancy's story is true," said Mr. Brownlow.

55
00:05:50.094 --> 00:05:59.173
"Is this man Monks really trying to cheat Oliver out of his inheritance? First we must ask Nancy if she's willing to point out Monks to us so we can deal with him."

56
00:05:59.174 --> 00:06:04.165
"That means we can't meet her until Sunday night—five days away," said Dr. Losberne.

57
00:06:04.166 --> 00:06:12.506
"But that will give me time to contact Harry Maylie, who will be a great help to us, I'm sure. He's Mrs. Maylie's son and a dear friend of Rose's."

58
00:06:12.507 --> 00:06:15.483
Rose blushed deeply but didn't say anything.

59
00:06:15.484 --> 00:06:22.141
"We will remain in London, of course," said Mrs. Maylie. "I don't care how long this takes."

60
00:06:22.142 --> 00:06:32.119
Mr. Brownlow stood up. "Now let's go to supper. Poor Oliver probably thinks we've tired of him and are plotting how to get rid of him."

